  "final_response": "- macOS – the “osxkeychain” mode caches credentials in the secure keychain attached to your system account. [credentials.001-credential-storage]  \n- This method stores the credentials on disk, never expires, and they are encrypted with the same system that stores HTTPS certificates and Safari auto‑fills. [credentials.001-credential-storage]  \n- When Git looks for credentials for a particular host, it queries the helpers in order and stops after the first answer is provided; when saving credentials, Git sends the username and password to all helpers in the list, which can decide what to do with them. [credentials.001-credential-storage]",
